1
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:03,377
Could this have happened
while we were sleeping?

2
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:04,600
To me and Giorno?

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,040
Mista and Trish?

4
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,877
What kind of messed up
voodoo crap is this?

5
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:12,372
Last I checked, people's minds
couldn't just trade bodies?

6
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,840
Stay your hands for now!

7
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,560
Wait, that can't be a stand!

8
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:19,939
Is that Zipperman?

9
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,440
Ain't no doubt!

10
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:23,960
It's Bucciarati!

11
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:31,677
In my eyes,

12
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:38,237
I'm going to turn back on my head

13
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,150
I'm going

14
00:00:39,233 --> 00:00:45,880
to

15
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:58,500
turn back on my head

16
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:55,857
Let's go!

17
00:01:55,940 --> 00:02:00,920
I'm going to go to the world,
and I'm going to go to the world.

18
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:04,405
I'm not going to die,
but I'm not going to die.

19
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:07,940
When I'm in my body, I'm going to die.

20
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:12,640
Hello, the beginning of the golden wind.

21
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,420
Oh, thank God!

22
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:28,997
Glad to have you back!

23
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:32,786
You even beat the boss to the
punch and tracked down the arrow!

24
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,780
I know that cadence.

25
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,097
That's how Narancia
speaks, if memory serves.

26
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:39,020
Am I right?

27
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:41,960
Huh? Yeah!

28
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,200
Thought so. And you two?

29
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,520
I'm Giorno.

30
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,540
And I'm Trish.

31
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:51,600
Impressive work, Bucciarati.

32
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:55,234
It appears you've already
pieced together what happened.

33
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:56,600
Wait a minute.

34
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,606
Are you the man we were
supposed to meet with?

35
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:02,540
I am Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

36
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:06,080
I died by Diavolo's hand.

37
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:11,617
However, after switching
souls with this turtle,

38
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:13,957
I was able to maintain a presence here,

39
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,517
like a ghost might haunt
the plane of the living.

40
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:18,880
And that over there is my stand.

41
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:23,397
With the arrow's power, he was
transformed into Chariot Requiem.

42
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:26,720
He is responsible for our displaced souls.

43
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:29,090
Wait,

44
00:03:29,173 --> 00:03:33,697
if my soul's in this body, then it's only
natural to conclude the boss is inside.

45
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,537
Yeah, don't worry about
him, he hasn't moved at all.

46
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,208
Guy's sleeping like a baby.

47
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,180
Might you be, Mista?

48
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,279
Yeah, I'm really glad to
see you're okay, old buddy.

49
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:46,717
Anyway, number seven's
got his eye on your body.

50
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:49,817
If it's so much as twitches,
we'll know immediately.

51
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,135
Again, he's out cold.

52
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:53,539
Might be a while before he gets up.

53
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,510
Bucciarati!

54
00:03:55,593 --> 00:03:57,259
Chariot Requiem's back on his feet!

55
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:01,257
We've already learned
how to use the arrow.

56
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:04,520
If we can just grab it,
this'll all be over!

57
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,033
What's this, Zipperman?

58
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,168
Oh man, what are you doing?

59
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,600
Quick, the arrow!

60
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,520
Requiem's going for it!

61
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:38,660
Not on my watch, you little bitch.

62
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,760
No, wait, something's wrong.

63
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:42,960
Miseria, did he?

64
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:49,997
I'm gonna kill you, you stupid ass!

65
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:53,877
That thick skull of yours is about to
become holier than a dog-shitting priest!

66
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,360
The pillar next to you! Mesa! Doc!

67
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,340
Spicy lady!

68
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:04,640
Die, you bastard!

69
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,477
I'm gonna blast your
ugly head open and paint

70
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:10,089
the streets with your
chunky noodle juices!

71
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,435
You'll never want to cut the shit out!

72
00:05:12,580 --> 00:05:14,777
What the hell do you think
you're doing, you moron?

73
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:15,920
Hey, stop it!

74
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,130
Huh?

75
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:20,660
What was I doing?

76
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:21,960
What happened?

77
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:23,100
It can't be!

78
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:26,440
Guys, over there!

79
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:29,140
Requiem, he's going for the arrow!

80
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,065
We can't just let him take it!

81
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,940
Oh, you gotta be freaking kidding me!

82
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,517
How did all that just happen?

83
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:47,440
If I were to guess, it's a
result of his frenetic state.

84
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:51,720
Not even I have seen Chariot show
such terrifying powers before.

85
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,080
But this much is clear.

86
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:58,520
In response to my subconscious
will, he's become a defensive stand.

87
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:02,431
As long as he lives, he'll
allow no one to touch the arrow.

88
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:04,860
To turn stands against their users.

89
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:08,577
Such a cunning defense mechanism
will prove challenging to defeat.

90
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:13,248
So not only can the arrow control all
our minds, it can pull tricks like this.

91
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,277
How are we supposed to get at it?

92
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,713
Dude is out of control!

93
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:20,917
Sure our stands might
be supercharged but that

94
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,597
just means if we try to
grab the arrow right now,

95
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,040
we'll get roasted alive

96
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:33,820
No holly you pipe down

97
00:06:38,140 --> 00:06:39,320
It'll be okay

98
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,750
Smirbles!

99
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:52,840
Whoever's inside, Bucciarati,
they're coming too!

100
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,200
My god, is it him?

101
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:58,077
We can worry about the arrow later.

102
00:06:58,160 --> 00:07:00,984
Get into place and don't
take your eyes off him!

103
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:05,311
Now, Mista, take a shot and make it count!

104
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:08,760
What did I say?

105
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,617
Put those bullets of yours to work!

106
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:15,171
Yeah, I heard, but dude, did you forget
that's your body I'd be shooting at?

107
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:16,871
There's no need to worry.

108
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:20,376
Golden Wind can patch up
bullet wounds without effort.

109
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:23,600
So shoot, all we gotta
do is incapacitate him.

110
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,915
That was your plan, right, Bucciarati?

111
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,193
Guys, he's on the move!

112
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:32,733
Come on, let's get him!

113
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:39,977
That should do it, fellas!

114
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:43,060
I don't think he'll be
charging at us anytime soon!

115
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:48,662
No one's showing up on my radar.

116
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:51,961
Looks like there won't be
any backup to deal with.

117
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,800
We did it.

118
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:01,000
Once we get the arrow,
this'll all be over.

119
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:06,414
And then, when we're back in
Napoli, it's off to school.

120
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:08,777
Hot damn, I'm already psyched.

121
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:12,837
The first thing I'll do is stuff my
face with an authentic margarita slice.

122
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,737
Might even top it with porcini's.

123
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:16,580
After that...

124
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:22,900
If I ever see Fugo again, he can
call me a kagakatsu all he wants.

125
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,800
I won't give two shits.

126
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:28,820
And even though Bakio's gone...

127
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:35,130
Trish!

128
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:37,760
I'll protect you till my dying breath!

129
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,060
That's a promise!

130
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,470
Narancia...

131
00:08:42,553 --> 00:08:45,920
Mista, just to be safe,
take out both of his legs.

132
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:47,460
Uh, yeah, sure.

133
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:50,417
Hey Trish, would you mind
handing me my bullets?

134
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:51,377
I want them all.

135
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:53,989
Just reach down into
my boot and grab them.

136
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:55,050
Uh, okay.

137
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:03,197
Hey, pick up the pace, will ya?

138
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,857
Those legs won't shoot themselves.

139
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:06,300
Wait, hold on a sec.

140
00:09:17,020 --> 00:09:18,520
Time jumped. Just now.

141
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:20,077
We skipped a few seconds.

142
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:20,990
I know.

143
00:09:21,073 --> 00:09:22,297
The bullets that fell on the ground.

144
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:24,277
Did anyone actually hear them land?

145
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,190
It can't be.

146
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:26,657
I was watching him closely.

147
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:30,317
Not once did I catch him move,
let alone evoke Emperor Crimson.

148
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,280
It just doesn't make any sense.

149
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:36,560
What other nefarious forces could
possibly be haunting us this time?

150
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:38,380
Listen, Trish.

151
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:40,507
I might need a little favor.

152
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:44,020
Could you go ahead and drop
one more bullet for me?

153
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:46,440
Oh, come on! Are you deaf?

154
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:49,857
Can you even count how many of them
are rolling around there right now?

155
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:51,040
The answer's four!

156
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,397
The absolute freaking worst!

157
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:55,257
I can't have that bullshit
number anywhere near me!

158
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:57,297
If they fell while you
were handing them over,

159
00:09:57,380 --> 00:10:00,968
then for the love of God, do me
a solid and drop another one!

160
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:03,017
How sure are we exactly?

161
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:04,512
That's Diavolo in there.

162
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:06,530
Hey, Trish.

163
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,097
Could you just remind me again?

164
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:09,520
When we all woke up,

165
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:12,677
you said you couldn't sense the
boss anywhere, isn't that right?

166
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:14,040
Well, what about now?

167
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:16,739
Are you picking up anything at all?

168
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:20,180
That cannot be the case!

169
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:24,297
You swapped with Narancia, and
accordingly Mista swapped with Trish.

170
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:27,321
It stands to reason Buterati
swapped with Diavolo.

171
00:10:27,560 --> 00:10:30,257
With Requiem's powers, they're
the only pairings that work.

172
00:10:30,340 --> 00:10:31,537
Yeah, I get what you're saying.

173
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:34,097
But none of that explains
why time just jumped.

174
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:38,768
That can only mean whoever's in that
body right now can't possibly be Diavolo.

175
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:41,495
Narancia, how does our perimeter look?

176
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:43,816
Are you able to detect anyone coming?

177
00:10:50,160 --> 00:10:50,990
Narancia?

178
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,800
Please, I'm begging you!

179
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,260
Just one more bullet!

180
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:12,757
Please, just drop one more!

181
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,670
You're driving me back!

182
00:11:13,753 --> 00:11:14,583
What the hell?

183
00:11:14,666 --> 00:11:17,077
Why couldn't I feel a
soul like I usually do?

184
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,689
It doesn't make any sense!

185
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,800
Out of the way! Move!

186
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,900
Let me through! Now!

187
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:24,340
Dammit, no!

188
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:25,519
That's impossible!

189
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:26,957
How on earth could he have?

190
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,880
Misha, scan the area right now!

191
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,922
Make sure there's no one around!

192
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:36,460
Narancia! Ahhhh!

193
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:39,010
Butcherati!

194
00:11:39,093 --> 00:11:40,697
Hurry up and get him down from there!

195
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:42,177
Don't just leave him like that!

196
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:43,217
Do something, goddammit!

197
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:44,397
You need to settle down!

198
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,477
Let me handle this!

199
00:11:45,560 --> 00:11:47,757
Please stay focused and
keep your gun at the ready!

200
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:48,937
He'll attack again!

201
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:51,491
We have to find him before he does, quick!

202
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:56,120
Go! Zipperman!

203
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:01,550
Heal him!

204
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:04,918
Pull those jam bars out of
there and get to work now!

205
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:13,905
The people outside the
Colosseum are waking up.

206
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:15,260
So where is he?

207
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,937
I can't sense him at all.

208
00:12:17,020 --> 00:12:18,196
It's like he's gone.

209
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,517
What else could have happened?

210
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:23,953
There's no way in hell he'd
just up and vanish like that.

211
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:27,735
Emperor Crimson's range is
two or three meters at most.

212
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:30,666
How then did he attack
us from way over there?

213
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,580
Well, alright! You did it!

214
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,840
Naraj is awake!

215
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:39,461
Welcome back, you little bastard!

216
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:41,076
How are you feeling?

217
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:43,440
Geez, you really scared us.

218
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,360
I'm sorry, Mista.

219
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:47,850
There's...

220
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:49,577
no one left...

221
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,680
in here.

222
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:54,220
It's empty.

223
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:57,348
The physical wounds he
suffered have healed.

224
00:12:58,380 --> 00:13:01,380
But still, Golden Wind
couldn't get to him in time.

225
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:02,937
He was...

226
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:04,980
he was already gone.

227
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:10,360
But I'm just not here.

228
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:19,000
His form, it's just an empty vessel now.

229
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:20,620
I can't find him.

230
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:23,140
His soul has left.

231
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,180
There's nothing here.

232
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:29,180
Try as I might, I can't bring him back.

233
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:30,920
I wasn't fast enough.

234
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:33,837
My soul could just slip
right back in if it wanted.

235
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:37,640
It could inhabit both bodies
without a problem, not even one.

236
00:13:38,220 --> 00:13:39,700
He's that empty.

237
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,430
Naracha!

238
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:57,340
It was all so sudden.

239
00:13:57,780 --> 00:13:59,545
None of us could have guessed.

240
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:15,240
I don't know.

241
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:07,920
That bastard!

242
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:09,751
Where could he be hiding?

243
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,577
This should never have happened!

244
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:15,400
The only explanation is if
there were two Diavolos!

245
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:18,210
Wait…

246
00:15:18,293 --> 00:15:20,257
The child that appeared before him…

247
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:21,640
Could it be?

248
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:23,797
Were both of them…

249
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:27,300
One physical body with
two different souls?

250
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:30,930
Butcherati!

251
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:31,910
I got it!

252
00:15:31,993 --> 00:15:34,140
Diavolo must have two personalities.

253
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,521
That is the only possible answer.

254
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:41,562
The one currently inside your body
is the young man I met earlier.

255
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:46,016
He and Diavolo may share a physical
body, but their souls are separate.

256
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:50,440
The human soul can be a
strange and delicate thing.

257
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:53,681
A traumatic childhood event
can easily fissure it.

258
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:58,660
As the individual grows, so too do
the fissures until the soul is split.

259
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:04,260
Over time, the second personality
distinguishes itself from the original,

260
00:16:04,580 --> 00:16:06,877
with one of them soon becoming dominant.

261
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:09,060
It's a well-documented disorder.

262
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:11,580
Listen to me.

263
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:14,180
What I'm saying is no mere conjecture.

264
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:17,037
Reports from across Europe
confirm that even one's

265
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:20,473
physical form will change as
the personalities alternate.

266
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:26,289
Requiem managed to extract these two
souls from the singular body they share.

267
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:30,881
One of them, the young man's, found
its way into Bucciarati's body.

268
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,920
The other one, however,
for reasons unknown,

269
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:37,141
has established itself in
a body we haven't found.

270
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:39,957
That's how Diavolo took us by surprise.

271
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:43,981
We didn't think he'd still be
roaming around in a different vessel.

272
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:45,880
This shit hurts my head.

273
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,059
Two personalities?

274
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:49,633
So that's what the boss has been hiding.

275
00:16:49,860 --> 00:16:52,977
As we speak, countless
civilians are awakening.

276
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:56,400
The haystack will soon
grow intractably large.

277
00:16:56,760 --> 00:17:01,054
I'm certain he'll pounce on us again,
and this time he'll finish the job.

278
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:03,380
That's one scenario.

279
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:08,560
However, it's just as likely
he's nowhere near us right now.

280
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:10,827
Diavolo wants the arrow too.

281
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:14,222
Which is why Narancia was
the first one targeted.

282
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:15,440
He's blinded us.

283
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:17,089
We've lost our only radar.

284
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:20,000
It's enabling him to move about freely.

285
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,477
No one can track him.

286
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,660
Not with Lil Balmer, anyway.

287
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:27,940
Yes, but even so, you must
keep your focus on the Arrow.

288
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:32,437
There's no point in going after
Emperor Crimson without its power.

289
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:36,167
That's precisely why we need to
locate Requiem before he does.

290
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:38,520
Do you remember which way he went?

291
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:39,540
To the West.

292
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:42,957
He's left a trail of people
regaining consciousness in his wake.

293
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:43,870
Wait a minute.

294
00:17:43,953 --> 00:17:46,177
Are you really planning to
chase him down right now?

295
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:48,457
What about your mangled body back there?

296
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:50,437
I avoided his vital organs.

297
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:54,080
He'll live, but he's not
getting up anytime soon.

298
00:17:54,420 --> 00:17:55,820
I made sure of that.

299
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,217
Stay put, okay?

300
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:11,817
You'll be safe here.

301
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:13,917
I won't let anyone hurt you again.

302
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,040
I promise.

303
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:22,440
And don't you worry, when it's
over we'll bring you home.

304
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:40,720
Watch out for anybody
coming near us. Let's go!

305
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:55,240
Trish what are you doing stay close right

306
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:15,440
Hey baby!

307
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:16,876
You're under arrest!

308
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:20,372
Come here and let me show you
how these cuffs look on you!

309
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,150
Hey!

310
00:19:23,233 --> 00:19:24,657
Is everything alright back there?

311
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:25,570
Yep.

312
00:19:25,653 --> 00:19:26,940
Just a false alarm.

313
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,637
This guy rushed at me so
I thought he was the boss.

314
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:31,485
But it was just a dumbass cop.

315
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:46,940
It's become increasingly clear to me.

316
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:51,060
Requiem has neither directional
nor emotional objectives.

317
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:56,337
Though we've closed in on him, he
hasn't once turned to look at me.

318
00:19:56,420 --> 00:19:58,949
There's no question
he's a living organism.

319
00:19:59,280 --> 00:20:04,045
Even if the resemblance he bears to some
rubber figurine would suggest otherwise.

320
00:20:09,060 --> 00:20:12,160
In his mind I've yet to
even register as a threat,

321
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:15,166
but even if I did he can
barely throw a punch.

322
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:17,951
Still his physical presence is quite real.

323
00:20:18,180 --> 00:20:20,768
I mean he's been seen
and touched hasn't he?

324
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:48,617
it's no good can't even get close it's not
just our stands anything we throw at it

325
00:20:48,700 --> 00:20:54,617
it sends flying right back in our faces
this arrow might really be untouchable it

326
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:58,497
doesn't matter how hard you try to reach
for it it's gonna push you back with just

327
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:02,077
as much force and here he comes again How

328
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:04,317
are we supposed to pick
this damn thing up?

329
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:06,080
It's like it's mocking us.

330
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:11,272
Hey, Requiem won't allow stand
users to pick up the arrow.

331
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:12,820
Which leads me to think,

332
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:16,457
what if a person without the gift
were to go ahead and try their luck?

333
00:21:16,540 --> 00:21:17,658
Would they succeed?

334
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:20,820
Well, what are your thoughts?

335
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:23,597
What do I look like, a stand scientist?

336
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:25,268
How the hell should I know?

337
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:30,120
Hey, guys!

338
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:31,460
Look, over here!

339
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:35,600
I've been reduced to a reptile
fighting to hold on to its dear soul.

340
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:38,000
That means I'm no longer a stand user.

341
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:39,880
It can't repel me.

342
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:45,430
Mista!

343
00:21:45,513 --> 00:21:46,499
The time has come!

344
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:49,080
Take the arrow and infill your stand now!

345
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:29,777
We are the power who'll
see the future Cause

346
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:34,280
we are the fighters
just fighting for a ride

347
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:57,960
Thank you.
